{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"temporary-pure-moth","creation_channel":"cli","description":"ROOT CAUSE (proven, cited).\n\nSymptom: pointing a model class at a local OpenAI-compatible server via the documented per-class endpoint — TOML 'trivial = { model=..., provider=\"openai\", endpoint=\"http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1\" }' or env REBAR_LLM_TRIVIAL_ENDPOINT=... — fails at run time with 'openai.OpenAIError: Missing credentials' (pydantic-ai's stock OpenAIProvider), instead of using rebar's OpenAI-compatible builder (which supplies api_key='not-needed' and withdraws supports_json_schema_output).\n\nMechanism: ClassSlot.endpoint is parsed (src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py _parse_slot, with dedicated env vars REBAR_LLM_{FRONTIER,STANDARD,TRIVIAL}_ENDPOINT) and documented (docs/llm-framework.md), but the ONLY consumer of any '.endpoint' is build_fallback_model (model_classes.py:403), which reads t.endpoint from FALLBACK targets only and hardcodes the PRIMARY candidate's endpoint to None. resolve_class / resolve_model_string return only 'provider:model', discarding the slot endpoint. Every op collapses the class onto cfg via replace(cfg, model=resolve_model_string(CLASS)) (enrich.py:82, epic_bug_screen.py:109, overlap/judge, plan_review, completion, code_review, workflow/runs), so cfg.base_url stays None. In runner.run, ProviderSession(cfg) then does NOT register the openai builder (it is registered only when cfg.base_url is set), so the primary takes the is_resolvable() lazy-string branch (runner.py ~381) and Agent(model_string) is built by pydantic-ai with no provider_factory -> stock OpenAIProvider -> requires OPENAI_API_KEY -> fails.\n\nAuthoritative contract violated: docs/llm-framework.md documents the per-class endpoint recipe as a working way to reach a local server, and the env table lists REBAR_LLM_<CLASS>_ENDPOINT as 'per-class OpenAI-compatible endpoint'.\n\nOnly working recipe today: top-level REBAR_LLM_BASE_URL (registers the builder + flips signed tier to best_effort). VALIDATED end-to-end against a local MLX server: enrich() returned a valid ticket_digest in ~35s.\n\nFIX (planned): at the single chokepoint runner.run — mirroring fallback_targets_for(resolved) — look up the slot whose primary resolves to 'resolved' and, when cfg.base_url is unset, apply that slot's endpoint to cfg.base_url so the builder registers, provenance records the host, and the tier flips to best_effort uniformly. RED->GREEN with a runner-level test.\n\nACCEPTANCE: a class slot / REBAR_LLM_<CLASS>_ENDPOINT with provider=openai and NO REBAR_LLM_BASE_URL routes the primary model through rebar's OpenAI-compatible builder (no OPENAI_API_KEY required); provenance base_url is set and tier=best_effort; existing base_url and fallback-endpoint behavior unchanged.","id":"6e70-3d3c-55da-4930","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["llm","local-models","provider-seam"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Per-class model-class endpoint (REBAR_LLM_<CLASS>_ENDPOINT / slot endpoint) is dropped for the primary model"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785882568047719001,"uuid":"01382474-30f3-4678-9d59-b0d7795a7578"}